#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046645} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536011} :activity/id #uuid "12416417-305e-5bcf-9b75-2b27fd54eeed" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050707 :topic/id #uuid "605a21e1-c415-5cc1-9181-c8f48db5f4ba" :topic/math-academy-id 6691} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536011 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308719 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9104f75-3823-5343-b10e-35210deee4b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}(4t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307163}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186307163} :answer-field/id #uuid "0de54400-c651-59cf-a2eb-bab2e9e63b82" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307571}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "411e1067-1bf2-5810-9a74-3f6443bfc23e" :question/math-academy-id "q-335058" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=4y(t)-4 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-4x(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n| $\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}$ and $g(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})} & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ 1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ 1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ 1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "1c1ad14e-74e6-51e6-a61f-0245fb4cfb09" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536036}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536026 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311584 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16a95f78-5388-52c8-81fd-1590793a0892" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{L2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308923} {:answer/id #uuid "458cdaa3-94ab-5b93-a888-b86e89c27d0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{L3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309279} {:answer/id #uuid "9e1acb02-1114-509d-910a-98a42188ebbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310024}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309279} :answer-field/id #uuid "0676014f-804f-59e5-bdff-81ae06e0bea9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310811} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1323f90a-02bd-56b9-8366-20c0593acd49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "evaluating at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308885} {:answer/id #uuid "3302abb0-2676-5e15-8a5e-e973064f4863" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "differentiating and using the sum rule" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309136} {:answer/id #uuid "5f4876b5-f5b7-5c5b-b070-7fabe22ebc4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{At}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309463} {:answer/id #uuid "6a8dd418-5f24-589e-bdee-aad054a11f19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "applying a change of variables" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309576}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308885} :answer-field/id #uuid "26b02ba4-09b1-554e-bc7e-4214b48c445f" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310889} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89378a2d-4acc-5784-bc7b-ecf07978d854" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "applying a change of variables" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309828} {:answer/id #uuid "9af06cd8-24db-5a45-96c2-35845daedc0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "substituting ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310001} {:answer/id #uuid "b46a0660-6e5d-5316-9901-267efc99e277" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "evaluating at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310209} {:answer/id #uuid "d09ffa81-f739-5099-a822-57634e2ce021" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "differentiating and using the product rule" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310425}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310001} :answer-field/id #uuid "2debb7d1-7e39-57b4-b320-31d7584ebebc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310914} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b52e291-66b0-5fa6-9e5e-f2456e04f53a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309073} {:answer/id #uuid "a9a78c95-4373-5610-a767-c7cb01964bcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310119} {:answer/id #uuid "be64fbcf-1a13-5e30-b6c8-eb59cd744f5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310287} {:answer/id #uuid "d60f5390-0372-51bc-8518-6a592260987c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310472}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309073} :answer-field/id #uuid "7bda7179-74ab-58d0-b1f2-f5c9e8cd0ec9" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311130}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "cebeb12c-43d2-5e26-85a3-7ca87fc81d5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-335396" :question/problem "Consider the inhomogeneous system  ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. A derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x(0)$ is presented below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let $y(t)={e}^{-At}x(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)={e}^{-At}g(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $y(t)-y(0)={\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $y(0)=x(0)$ \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $y(t)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$  \n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ ${e}^{At}y(t)={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${e}^{At}y(t)=x(t)$\n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from line\n{{field-2}}\nby integrating both sides from $0$ to \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by  \n{{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Starting from\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nin $\\text{L2}$ and substituting ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)$ from the original system gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}(Ax(t)+g(t)) \\\\  & =-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}g(t) \\\\  & ={e}^{-At}g(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by $\\text{substituting }{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t).$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ Integrating ${y}^{′}(t)={e}^{-At}g(t)$ from $0$ to $t$ in $\\text{L3}$ yields\n\n$$\ny(t)-y(0)={\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nSo, $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L3}$ by integrating both sides from $0$ to $t.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L5}.$ Evaluating $y(t)={e}^{-At}x(t)$ at $t=0$ gives\n\n$$\ny(0)={e}^{-A\\cdot 0}x(0)=Ix(0)=x(0).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L5}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{evaluating at }t=0.$"} :step/id #uuid "6904603d-53fd-531b-aed9-20fdeb45db7b" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536050}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536029 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370330 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1e5b2a0-9a4f-5861-a763-8728282aaeea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "evaluating at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370332} {:answer/id #uuid "e49141e3-96c9-507d-8ff6-995cb359a742" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "applying a change of variables" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370333} {:answer/id #uuid "fafd991f-b8f7-52d0-a95d-3dd5ccc37f13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "substituting ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370334} {:answer/id #uuid "8f7fb611-e6df-5c1b-8723-31f8eacf9ce3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "differentiating and using the product rule" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370335}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370335} :answer-field/id #uuid "28cbc50b-02c4-5424-9f1b-7fce11101a13" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370331} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2328997d-553e-53f3-857d-0f409d47bc1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "evaluating at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370337} {:answer/id #uuid "f2ae3eef-7d16-59e8-a6a7-53ac0338de51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "applying a change of variables" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370338} {:answer/id #uuid "77b7c353-0de8-54a4-b44f-0ab8d3a98105" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "substituting ${e}^{At}y(t)=x(t)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370339} {:answer/id #uuid "0a07471f-1be3-5e6b-9c9e-47c1761506c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{At}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370340}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370339} :answer-field/id #uuid "56d1136b-14bb-539e-8254-4bd02fc30b7e" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370336} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ccfd149-f7ec-54f1-a8ae-cea09d647402" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{At}y(t)=x(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370342} {:answer/id #uuid "6eedfdc4-31bc-5db4-9a15-3b9895ccc503" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y(0)=x(0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370343} {:answer/id #uuid "1e148004-ccba-5bcf-85ab-daff0d8a141b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370344} {:answer/id #uuid "4490b8c6-05d5-5e52-bbbb-8cca370cbec8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y(t)={e}^{-At}x(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370345}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370343} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf5e4979-0753-56be-820a-d3135a232e65" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370341} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91463c56-f813-584e-a711-1bbb5e2c2dfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370347} {:answer/id #uuid "6b9771cf-2af2-5c52-924c-4e617298a6f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{L4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370348} {:answer/id #uuid "8c7938c4-9daf-50a9-843d-f8425a468cbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{L3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370349}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370348} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d6f2ff9-e999-5c34-9262-e524815fe287" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370346}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "41091ce1-ce64-5374-9293-b98c681300fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-335405" :question/problem "Consider the inhomogeneous system  ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. A derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x(0)$ is presented below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let $y(t)={e}^{-At}x(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)={e}^{-At}g(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $y(t)-y(0)={\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $y(0)=x(0)$ \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $y(t)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$  \n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ ${e}^{At}y(t)={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${e}^{At}y(t)=x(t)$\n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line\n{{field-2}}\nby substituting \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L9}$ follows from line $\\text{L7}$ by  \n{{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Differentiating $y(t)={e}^{-At}x(t)$ and applying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =({e}^{-At})^{′}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(-A){e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{differentiating and using the product rule}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L4}$, $\\text{L5}$, and $\\text{L6}.$ From $\\text{L4}$ we have\n\n$$\ny(t)-y(0)={\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nUsing $y(0)=x(0)$ from $\\text{L5}$, this becomes\n\n$$\ny(t)-x(0)={\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nso\n\n$$\ny(t)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L4}$ by substituting $y(0)=x(0).$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L7}$, $\\text{L8}$, and $\\text{L9}.$ From $\\text{L8}$ we know that\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}y(t)=x(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${e}^{At}y(t)=x(t)$ into\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}y(t)={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s\n$$\n\nfrom $\\text{L7}$ gives\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L9}$ follows from $\\text{L7}$ by $\\text{substituting }{e}^{At}y(t)=x(t).$"} :step/id #uuid "7a5de0ff-7990-5b8c-9f62-a36d2977e2f1"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536036 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535950 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4f64bf3-528b-508d-afe7-7fb41040696f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\cos(t)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535760}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535760} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0cddfae-ecf5-50fd-9bfc-04c2102bb55f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535905}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5cb555db-6a59-509d-947e-27c4f1a2a7e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-335062" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=y(t)+1 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"120px\">$2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]$ and $g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})} & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}]}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "98ff146f-1e74-5987-92d5-7e14960c7748" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536026}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536050 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535981 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42b3ed5c-fad2-5cc4-8d0b-6a6baccca373" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{At}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535537} {:answer/id #uuid "80c6f160-e91a-566a-bbbc-ef9f781ae2c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "applying a change of variables" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535638} {:answer/id #uuid "b43d995f-de71-5c35-a7e4-7783c88a1a2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "integrating both sides" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535711} {:answer/id #uuid "c752c0eb-512f-538b-978e-3d7df287dd00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "evaluating at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535734}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535537} :answer-field/id #uuid "070b8c00-5b6b-5a44-a8d1-5e51fc41aa76" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535834} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a8dbdd8-8dfd-5db1-b4cd-9bab37d71d9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{At}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535453} {:answer/id #uuid "55d4713b-294f-5d25-89d5-a2f64e40b04a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "evaluating at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535570} {:answer/id #uuid "68e03ce5-612b-5030-b312-5b4ab7a5ec29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "differentiating and using the sum rule" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535600} {:answer/id #uuid "864e8d51-dded-5420-af14-e1f984c4c0a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "applying a change of variables" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535649}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535570} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdcdafbc-2a00-5bc3-a5dd-993258a4e62f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535904} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4be10430-59d1-599e-b689-c9308f9eceb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "differentiating and using the product rule" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535546} {:answer/id #uuid "4c3b2da4-577b-58b9-8f03-aec6ff89a8b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "applying a change of variables" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535547} {:answer/id #uuid "8912a77d-a8a2-5b0f-90ee-99de77bd7394" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "substituting ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535653} {:answer/id #uuid "eda14cbf-71c6-5101-91f3-6c716e888eef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "evaluating at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535801}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535546} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1dc9399-c403-56eb-8f48-08331960ca43" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535919}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ace7005c-d6c8-5219-91cc-32f47feb4972" :question/math-academy-id "q-335403" :question/problem "Consider the inhomogeneous system  ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. A derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x(0)$ is presented below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let $y(t)={e}^{-At}x(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)={e}^{-At}g(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $y(t)-y(0)={\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $y(0)=x(0)$ \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $y(t)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$  \n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ ${e}^{At}y(t)={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${e}^{At}y(t)=x(t)$\n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by  \n{{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ follows from line $\\text{L6}$ by  \n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Differentiating $y(t)={e}^{-At}x(t)$ and applying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =({e}^{-At})^{′}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(-A){e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{differentiating and using the product rule}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L5}.$ Evaluating $y(t)={e}^{-At}x(t)$ at $t=0$ gives\n\n$$\ny(0)={e}^{-A\\cdot 0}x(0)=Ix(0)=x(0).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L5}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{evaluating at }t=0.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L6}$ and $\\text{L7}.$ Multiplying both sides of\n\n$$\ny(t)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,ds\n$$\n\nfrom $\\text{L6}$ by ${e}^{At}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At}y(t) & ={e}^{At}x(0)+{e}^{At}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L7}$ follows from $\\text{L6}$ by $\\text{multiplying both sides by }{e}^{At}.$"} :step/id #uuid "f824fb6b-0584-52aa-83b5-662d7f07a788" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536029}}] :activity/title "Solving Inhomogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Matrix Methods" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535426}]}
